			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="311" width="290" height="25" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="12" field="technology" nome="Technology"/>
			</layout>
			<!--
				The thirteenth knowledge and a typed row on ONE top, and the renderer shows exactly
				one of them (SPEC I123b, V371b). Knowledges is the only column an era changes the
				length of: Modern Nights and the Classical Age list thirteen, the Victorian era and
				the Dark Ages twelve. An era borrows a trait from no other era (Q34), so the two
				short eras pay for the row with a name the player types instead.

				One top and not two: a second top would leave 25px of hole in whichever era hides
				the upper row, which is the gap this pairing exists to close. It is the hidden pair
				MeritPicked already runs (SPEC V354a), one row wider.

				Authored state is the Victorian era like every other row here (SPEC V76), so the
				named half ships hidden and the typed half ships visible. Its field is `computer`
				because that is the one knowledge no twelve-name era lists: the authored column
				stays one field per row even with the hidden one counted.
			-->
			<layout name="dynAbilRow_knowledges_13" visible="false" left="20" top="336" width="290" height="25" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="13" field="computer" nome="Computer"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dynAbilFill_knowledges_13" left="20" top="336" width="290" height="25" >
				<CustomAbility field="customKnowledge_3"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="361" width="290" height="25" >
				<CustomAbility field="customKnowledge_1"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="386" width="290" height="25" >
				<CustomAbility field="customKnowledge_2"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<!--
			Bottom row, two columns now, ending at y=760 (SPEC T78/T79, V69):
			  VIRTUES (310-600, y 460-586) over HUMANITY & WILLPOWER (310-600, y 596-760)
			  SPECIALTIES (615-905, y 460-760, SPEC I14) | HEALTH (920-1210)

			Every one of them takes its x from the column above it since the 50th round
			(SPEC V168): Virtues and Humanity from TALENTS, SPECIALTIES from SKILLS, HEALTH
			from KNOWLEDGES. They rose 50 with the same round, which is what the ability
			columns gave back when they stopped carrying a black tail (SPEC V171).

			Virtues and Humanity are 290 wide, not 410: their content is a 250px track (a 125px
			label plus 5 dots, or 10 bare dots), so 410 left a wide empty margin and made the
			Humanity/Willpower dots read as right-aligned. 290 = 250 + a 20px margin each side,
			which centres both tracks. The 120px freed went to HEALTH.

			HEALTH is 290 wide because 150 was not enough for its own labels: "Wounded (-2)" is
			"Ferido Gravemente (-2)" in pt, ~143px in a 125px checkBox. V16 only measures
			<label>, never <checkBox>, so that overflow was never flagged by the gate.

			Faith is gone from this tab on purpose: `faith_1`..`_5` are now the dots of the
			TRUE FAITH row on the Powers tab, so a saved sheet keeps its rating (SPEC V35).
		-->
		<layout left="345" top="541" width="330" height="126">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="20" top="15" width="290" height="20" text="VIRTUES" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<layout left="40" top="36" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="conscience" nome="Conscience"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="40" top="61" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="selfControl" nome="Self-Control"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="40" top="86" width="250" height="25" >
				<Attribute field="courage" nome="Courage"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<layout left="345" top="672" width="330" height="184">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>

			<!--
				HUMANITY became ROAD in the 125th round (SPEC I99a). Only the LABEL moved: the ten
				dots are still `humanity_1`..`_10`, so a saved sheet keeps its rating (SPEC V2, V5) -
				the same trade `retainers`->GUIDES and `items`->TRANSPORTATION already made.

				`cboRoad` sits ABOVE the track, so the box title says what the track IS and the combo
				says WHICH road. It leads on `Humanity` and carries no empty item: a character with no
				road IS on Humanity, which is the V15 exception SPEC C declares (SPEC I99b).

				The bearing line is glued to the bottom of the dots at top=99 - the dots close exactly
				there - because the request asked for it with no gap. Two labels and not one padded
				string: V11 forbids padding to line a column up, and the modifier is its own column
				(SPEC I99e). They carry the `dyn` prefix and NO text=: that prefix is what keeps the
				WoD20.6 language traversal off a Lua-written label, which would otherwise snapshot the
				authored English and restore it stale (SPEC V31) - the same reason the health rows use
				it. SPEC I99e names them lbl*, and that spelling is wrong for a Lua-written label.

				cboRoad is 290 and not 250: the ruler wants 241px for `The Path of Power and the Inner
				Voice` plus the 24px arrow (SPEC V312), so the dot track's width would clip it. It
				spans the box interior instead.

				WILLPOWER fell 49 and the box grew 26 to fit, which is the second branch the user chose
				in Q8. SPECIALTIES and the avatar grew the SAME 26 in the same commit - V69 reads all
				three closing on one y, and moving one alone turns it red (SPEC I99i, I99j).
			-->
			<!-- The pair is CENTRED as a group, and the group's width moves with the language:
			     `ROAD` is four characters and `CAMINHO` is seven (SPEC I128b/I128c, V380, T864,
			     user 2026-08-31 ask 6). renderRoadPair writes both lefts and the label's width
			     from ROAD_LABEL_W at every language change.

			     What is AUTHORED here is the LONGER of the two - pt, 65px at left=29 - and not
			     the English the sheet is written in: V16/V25 and V351(c) read the XML, and a
			     label authored at the English width would be a clipped `CAMINHO` sitting in the
			     file waiting for someone to open the sheet in pt. Declaring the worst case and
			     letting the renderer shrink it is what HEALTH already does with its ten-row
			     height (SPEC V49) - the file says the biggest it can ever be, and Lua takes it
			     down. Nothing is measured against the English case except the screen. -->
			<label name="lblRoad" left="29" top="15" width="65" height="24" text="ROAD" horzTextAlign="trailing" vertTextAlign="center"/>
			<button name="btnQroad" left="99" top="15" width="20" height="24" text="?" onClick="popOpen(self, 'Road', sheet['road'], nil, 'road');"/>
			<button name="dynroad" left="124" top="15" width="176" height="24" fontSize="12" text="Select Road" onClick="mfOpen(self, 'road', 'road', 'Road');"/>
			<!-- The typed twin, one field and two widgets with exactly one visible (SPEC I71, V274).
			     Authored state IS the flag off - visible AND enabled - because invisible-and-enabled
			     still takes Tab focus, which no screenshot shows (SPEC V274c, V274d). -->
			<edit name="edtRoad" left="124" top="15" width="176" height="24" field="road" visible="false" enabled="false"/>
			<layout left="40" top="44" width="250" height="25" >
				<Advantages field="humanity"/>
			</layout>
			<!-- ONE label and not two (user 2026-08-29): the bearing and its modifier read as a
			     single centred sentence, which two labels cannot do - each would centre in its own
			     half and the pair would drift off centre as the name grows. This REVOKES the
			     "the modifier is its own column" half of I99e; V11 is untouched, because what
			     joins them is a real space and a real parenthesis, not padding.
			
			     0.80 is neither of the two dimming numbers of I43/V244 and is not trying to be:
			     those two say "read-only", this one is the emphasis the user asked for on a line
			     that was never editable. Authored, so no runtime write reaches V244. -->
			<label name="dynBearingName" left="20" top="69" width="290" height="20" horzTextAlign="center" opacity="0.80"/>

			<!-- 99 and not 94: the bearing line closes on 89, so the gap is 10 (SPEC I128a, T864,
			     user 2026-08-31 ask 4). It was 20 until I124d took it to 5 on a "shrink it a lot,
			     but still a small space" - and 5 is the hairline a box title gets, which read as
			     no space at all under a line of text. Half way back is what the ask asked for.
			     The box does not grow for it. The foot under the willpower row is the 15 every
			     box on the sheet takes since T913, and T914 is what brought this one to it
			     (SPEC I138, V393, user 2026-09-02). -->
			<label left="20" top="99" width="290" height="20" text="WILLPOWER" horzTextAlign="center"/>
			<layout left="40" top="124" width="250" height="45" >
				<Willpower field="willpower"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<!--
			HEALTH is positional now (SPEC T96): row N is the Nth damage box, `health_1`..`_10`.
			The old semantic names (bruised/hurt/injured/...) are gone - they could not express a
			track where the label repeats (four "Bruised" rows at 10 levels), so they are declared
			orphans in SPEC I3 and a sheet saved before this loses its health marks. Requested.

			The labels carry NO text= here: renderHealthTrack() on the root form writes them from
			HEALTH_LEVELS, already translated, and hides the rows past the chosen length. The
			`dyn` name prefix is what keeps the WoD20.6 language traversal off them - it snapshots
			authored English once, and would restore a stale label after a length change (V31).

			Each row is a named layout so the renderer can hide label and mark box together; the
			mark itself is a four-symbol box, see the HealthRow template (SPEC T116).

			height=306 is the TEN-row case on purpose (SPEC V49): the renderer shrinks the box to
			fit the chosen track length, so the file always declares the tallest it can ever be
			and the box-overlap check (V40), which reads this file and not the running sheet,
			keeps measuring the worst case.

			Title is 205 wide, not 280, to leave room for the level combo. That is under the 80%
			the gate treats as a full-width section title, so V27 still holds for this box.
			245px per row because "Wounded (-2)" is "Ferido Gravemente (-2)" in pt (V38 / B17).
		-->
		<layout name="dynHealth_box" left="1015" top="541" width="330" height="325">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<!-- How long the track is moved to the storyteller's box in the 82nd round (SPEC I35,
			     V234): it was never the player's call, and it was the last thing on this sheet
			     held by two widgets on one field. The title spans the whole box now that it no
			     longer shares the row with a combo, so horzTextAlign centres it on the BOX. -->
			<label left="20" top="15" width="290" height="20" text="HEALTH" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<layout name="dynHealth_row1" left="42" top="47" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="1"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row2" left="42" top="74" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="2"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row3" left="42" top="101" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="3"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row4" left="42" top="128" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="4"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row5" left="42" top="155" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="5"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row6" left="42" top="182" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="6"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row7" left="42" top="209" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="7"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row8" left="42" top="236" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="8"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row9" left="42" top="263" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="9"/></layout>
			<layout name="dynHealth_row10" left="42" top="290" width="246" height="20"><HealthRow num="10"/></layout>
		</layout>

		<!--
			SPECIALTIES (SPEC I14, T388) took the corner the 46th round emptied when BACKGROUNDS
			moved to the Traits tab. It takes both x edges from the column above it - SKILLS, the
			way V168 had it before the 157th round put it beside KNOWLEDGES and T908 brought it
			back (SPEC V375, I136c). What it does NOT do any more is close on the bottom line:
			its height is content plus a 20px foot and nothing else, which is the owner ask of
			2026-09-02 and what V393 pins (SPEC V376, I136d, Q47).

			TEN rows: the first at 41 on the title hairline and a pitch of 25 puts the tenth at
			266..291, and the 20 under it is the foot - 311 in all. A table with no free slot
			says so with a pop-up rather than dropping the grant (SPEC V146/V153).

			No column headings: the box has one title and the three columns explain themselves.
			The row is 270 wide inside a 290 box - 150 for the trait, 85 for the text, 25 for the
			dot, 5 between each. It was 300 in a 320 box until the 50th round narrowed the box to
			match KNOWLEDGES; the 30 came out of the free-text field and not out of the picker,
			which has to show "Empatia com Animais" at 19 characters (SPEC V16).
		-->
		<layout left="680" top="541" width="330" height="315">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="20" top="15" width="290" height="20" text="SPECIALTIES" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<layout left="35" top="36" width="260" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="1"/></layout>
			<layout left="35" top="61" width="260" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="2"/></layout>
			<layout left="35" top="86" width="260" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="3"/></layout>
			<layout left="35" top="111" width="260" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="4"/></layout>
			<layout left="35" top="136" width="260" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="5"/></layout>
			<layout left="35" top="161" width="260" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="6"/></layout>
			<layout left="35" top="186" width="260" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="7"/></layout>
			<layout left="35" top="211" width="260" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="8"/></layout>
			<layout left="35" top="236" width="260" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="9"/></layout>
			<layout left="35" top="261" width="260" height="25"><SpecialityRow num="10"/></layout>
		</layout>

	</scrollBox>

	<!--
		The health labels are written by Lua, so they need re-rendering whenever the track length
		or the language changes. Two independent entry points on purpose (SPEC V19 / V33): the
		dataLink covers later edits, onNodeReady covers the sheet simply being opened.
	-->
	<dataLink fields="{'healthLevels', 'language'}" onChange="renderHealthTrack(self, 'dynHealth_'); renderRoadPair(self);"/>

	<!-- The experience box is worked out, not stored (SPEC I11): it follows the one saved
	     number, and every dot on this tab redraws it through the guard. -->
	<dataLink field="xpTotal" onChange="renderXPBoxes(self);"/>

	<!-- A free speciality is locked (SPEC V161/V164), and which rows are free is written in
	     the stamps. Watching them covers the grant that happened on ANOTHER client at the
	     table: the field arrives over the NDB, and the row locks here too.

	     `xpFree` carries no widget by design - it is Lua-owned, the declared exception to
	     V8 (SPEC I3, B25). -->
	<dataLink field="xpFree" onChange="renderSpecialities(self);"/>

	<event name="onShow">
		wodTrace("WoD20.1.onShow");
		renderXPBoxes(self);
	</event>

	<event name="onNodeReady">
		renderHealthTrack(self, 'dynHealth_');
		renderRoadPair(self);
		renderXPBoxes(self);
		renderSpecialities(self);
	</event>
</form>
